### goat-errors — English (en), the arbiter
### Generated from ops/errors/catalog.yaml by ops/ci/check-error-catalog.py --write; do not edit.
### Keys: <code>-title, <code>-what, <code>-cause-<n> (n from 1).

e-profile-missing-title = no profile for this context
e-profile-missing-what = goat was run before `goat profile init`, or the context named has no profile.toml, certificate or key.
e-profile-missing-cause-1 = the bundle was never installed on this machine
e-profile-missing-cause-2 = the bundle was installed into a different context than the one in use
e-profile-denied-title = the profile exists but this user cannot read it
e-profile-denied-what = the profile directory is there and permission was denied reading it, typically a root-owned 0700 ~/.goat probed without sudo, or bare sudo that reset $HOME to /root.
e-profile-denied-cause-1 = the profile was created as root
e-profile-denied-cause-2 = bare `sudo goat …` looked in /root/.goat
e-bundle-invalid-title = the bundle did not verify
e-bundle-invalid-what = at `goat profile init` the bundle's structure, signature or expiry failed. The help line says which of the three.
e-bundle-invalid-cause-1 = a truncated or wrong download (malformed CBOR)
e-bundle-invalid-cause-2 = a signing CA this machine does not trust
e-bundle-invalid-cause-3 = an expired bundle
e-off-mesh-title = not connected to the mesh
e-off-mesh-what = the local mesh client reports no connected tunnel, so nothing on the goatnet is reachable.
e-off-mesh-cause-1 = the mesh client is stopped or logged out
e-off-mesh-cause-2 = this device was never enrolled
e-off-mesh-cause-3 = the device is on a network that blocks the mesh
e-clock-skew-title = the device clock is wrong
e-clock-skew-what = the device clock differs from the management server's authenticated HTTPS Date by more than 60 seconds, so certificates cannot be judged valid.
e-clock-skew-cause-1 = the clock drifted while the device was off or offline
e-router-unreachable-title = the Zenoh router did not answer
e-router-unreachable-what = the configured router's TCP path or Zenoh session timed out or could not be reached.
e-router-unreachable-cause-1 = the mesh tunnel is up but the route to the router is not
e-router-unreachable-cause-2 = the router service is down on its host
e-router-unreachable-cause-3 = the endpoint in the profile is stale
e-cert-expired-title = the mTLS certificate is outside its validity
e-cert-expired-what = the local certificate is expired, not yet valid, or was rejected by the router.
e-cert-expired-cause-1 = the certificate's validity interval has passed
e-cert-expired-cause-2 = the device clock is wrong (see E_CLOCK_SKEW)
e-doctor-inconclusive-title = doctor saw a failure it cannot narrow
e-doctor-inconclusive-what = a local TLS or configuration failure, or a session rejection, without enough evidence for one cause.
e-doctor-inconclusive-cause-1 = router-side admission refused this identity
e-doctor-inconclusive-cause-2 = a local TLS setup problem the probe cannot distinguish from the router's
e-portal-unreachable-title = the portal API did not answer
e-portal-unreachable-what = the portal was not reachable for network reasons (DNS, TCP or TLS), not an authorization failure.
e-portal-unreachable-cause-1 = the portal host is not reachable over the mesh from this device
e-portal-unreachable-cause-2 = mesh DNS is not resolving the portal name
e-portal-not-found-title = the portal answered that what was named is not registered
e-portal-not-found-what = the portal is up and answered HTTP 404 for the request path shown: the org, topic, schema, machine or person the command named does not exist there. An answer, not a network fault.
e-portal-not-found-cause-1 = a typo in the org prefix, topic key or handle
e-portal-not-found-cause-2 = the thing is registered on another goatnet than the active context's
e-portal-not-found-cause-3 = it was removed, or never created
e-portal-rate-limited-title = the portal is rate-limiting this client
e-portal-rate-limited-what = the portal is up and answered HTTP 429: this client sent too many requests. The hint carries the portal's Retry-After when it sent one.
e-portal-rate-limited-cause-1 = a script calling goat in a tight loop
e-portal-rate-limited-cause-2 = an older goat whose `topic ls` with no prefix made one request per org
e-portal-server-error-title = the portal failed on its own side
e-portal-server-error-what = the portal is up and answered HTTP 5xx for the request path shown. Nothing on this device's network or credential is at fault.
e-portal-server-error-cause-1 = the portal or a service behind it (its database, the registry) is failing
e-portal-server-error-cause-2 = the portal is restarting during a deploy (often a 502 or 503)
e-portal-refused-title = the portal refused the request
e-portal-refused-what = the portal is up and answered a non-2xx status no command curates (a 400, 405, 410, 413 or 422) for the request path shown.
e-portal-refused-cause-1 = this goat build and the portal are at different API versions
e-portal-refused-cause-2 = a value the command sent is one the portal does not accept
e-portal-bad-response-title = the portal answered in a shape this goat build does not understand
e-portal-bad-response-what = the portal returned 2xx but the body did not deserialize. The portal is healthy; the CLI and the portal are at different versions.
e-portal-bad-response-cause-1 = goat is behind the portal
e-portal-bad-response-cause-2 = the portal deployed ahead of the CLI
e-token-invalid-title = the portal rejected the token
e-token-invalid-what = the portal accepted the connection and refused the bearer token (HTTP 401): the credential itself is expired or misissued.
e-token-invalid-cause-1 = the token in ~/.goat/contexts/<name>/portal.token has expired
e-token-invalid-cause-2 = the token belongs to another goatnet
e-portal-forbidden-title = the portal refused this identity
e-portal-forbidden-what = HTTP 403 to the probe. The token was accepted; the identity lacks the access.
e-portal-forbidden-cause-1 = the active context is a different identity than you meant
e-portal-forbidden-cause-2 = the grant for this surface was never made
e-not-admin-title = an operator-only action without operator authority
e-not-admin-what = a `goat admin` action was refused, client-side (no operator credentials in the profile) or by the portal/NetBird API (HTTP 403, nothing changed).
e-not-admin-cause-1 = the profile is using the vp_ participant token, not the op_ operator key
e-not-admin-cause-2 = the role is not authorized for this action
e-topic-conflict-title = the topic already exists
e-topic-conflict-what = `goat topic create` was asked for a name that is already registered.
e-topic-conflict-cause-1 = someone created it first
e-topic-conflict-cause-2 = a re-run of a create that already succeeded
e-machine-unresolved-title = the machine named is not exactly one enrolled machine
e-machine-unresolved-what = a `goat machine` verb was given a handle or slot anchor that matches no enrolled machine this profile can see, or a handle that matches machines under more than one custodian. Nothing was changed.
e-machine-unresolved-cause-1 = a typo in the handle
e-machine-unresolved-cause-2 = the machine is under another custodian's custody, which a non-operator profile cannot see
e-machine-unresolved-cause-3 = the machine was revoked
e-machine-unresolved-cause-4 = two custodians each enrolled a machine with the same handle
e-mesh-peer-unresolved-title = the enrolled machine has no single mesh peer
e-mesh-peer-unresolved-what = the machine is enrolled, but no NetBird peer carries its name, or several do. A machine's peer is named `machine-<handle>-<host>` by its setup key, or `<handle>` when renamed by hand. Nothing was changed.
e-mesh-peer-unresolved-cause-1 = the machine never joined the mesh with its setup key
e-mesh-peer-unresolved-cause-2 = the peer was renamed off its handle in the NetBird dashboard
e-mesh-peer-unresolved-cause-3 = the machine joined twice, leaving a stale peer beside the live one
e-netbird-failed-title = the NetBird management API call failed
e-netbird-failed-what = a call to the goatnet's NetBird management API did not succeed for a reason other than authorization, so nothing was changed. The help line carries the status or the transport error.
e-netbird-failed-cause-1 = the NetBird admin token was rejected (HTTP 401)
e-netbird-failed-cause-2 = the management server is unreachable from this machine
e-netbird-failed-cause-3 = the management server answered an unexpected status
e-netbird-failed-cause-4 = the peer record lacked a setting the update has to send back unchanged
e-acl-declaration-missing-title = no ACL declaration was supplied
e-acl-declaration-missing-what = `goat acl test` or `goat warrant` needs the goatnet's netbird_acl_taxonomy.yml and netbird_acl_matrix.yml and found them nowhere. goat carries no deployment's declaration, so it stops rather than check other rules.
e-acl-declaration-missing-cause-1 = the command ran outside a checkout and the context holds no declaration
e-acl-declaration-missing-cause-2 = the goatnet does not serve its declaration at get.<site>/acl/, so `goat context refresh` fetched none
